# EXTERNALS — the values that can't be generated (third-party registration). Copy to
# `deploy/prod/secrets.local.env` (GITIGNORED), fill in, then run:
#     ./scripts/bootstrap-secrets.sh
# It merges these into the ONE Secrets Manager secret `alethia/prod/env`. Nothing here
# goes into GitHub. Do NOT quote values — everything after the first `=` is the value.
# Internal secrets (BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, DB passwords, …) are auto-generated — omit them.
#
# GO-LIVE MAP — what's needed for what:
#   REQUIRED to boot:  CLOUDFLARE_* + HCLOUD_TOKEN + HCLOUD_FLEET_TOKEN + PUBLIC_APP_URL.
#     (HCLOUD_SSH_KEYS is OPTIONAL — the runner self-registers over HTTP; leave blank for no SSH key.)
#   OPTIONAL features (leave blank to keep off): the cloud connectors, inactive Stripe billing,
#     support Slack, analytics. Each section below says what unset does.
#   The managed-cloud connector values (Azure app id, AWS role ARN) don't exist until you run a ONE-TIME
#   setup — see docs → Self-hosting → Managed cloud connectors (/self-hosting/managed-cloud-connectors).
#   Every key here is [ext]; commented (#) keys are optional overrides with a working default.

# ── Cloudflare (tunnel + DNS) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Token scopes: Account·Cloudflare Tunnel:Edit, Zone·DNS:Edit, Zone·Zone:Read,
# Account·Account Settings:Read (zone = alethialabs.io).
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# ── Hetzner (two separate projects/tokens) ───────────────────────────────────
HCLOUD_TOKEN=            # control-plane project, Read & Write
HCLOUD_FLEET_TOKEN=      # fleet project, Read & Write
HCLOUD_SSH_KEYS=         # OPTIONAL: key NAMES or IDs in the FLEET project; unknown skipped (not fatal)
# HCLOUD_SERVER_TYPE=cax21   # optional — fleet VM size; default cax21

# NOTE: the CI→box deploy SSH keypair is AUTO-GENERATED by bootstrap-secrets.sh (ed25519)
# and stored in the vault — you don't provide it. (Bring-your-own: run with
# DEPLOY_SSH_KEY_FILE=./your_key to import an existing private key instead.)

# ── App origin ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://alethialabs.io

# ── OAuth (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GitHub OAuth App callback: https://alethialabs.io/api/auth/callback/github
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Google OAuth client callback: https://alethialabs.io/api/auth/callback/google
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GitLab application (genericOAuth). Redirect URI: https://alethialabs.io/api/auth/oauth2/callback/gitlab
GITLAB_APPLICATION_ID=
GITLAB_SECRET=
# Bitbucket OAuth consumer (genericOAuth). Callback URL: https://alethialabs.io/api/auth/oauth2/callback/bitbucket
BITBUCKET_KEY=
BITBUCKET_SECRET=

# ── Managed cloud platform identity (optional) ───────────────────────────────
# All four managed clouds are KEYLESS and issuer-direct — the customer's IAM role / WIF pool / RAM OIDC
# provider / managed identity trusts Alethia's own OIDC issuer directly (no static keys, no platform AWS
# account). ALL FOUR need NOTHING here — availability tracks the OIDC signing key alone.
# See docs → Self-hosting → Managed cloud connectors.
# Azure: there is NO platform Entra app and NO ALETHIA_AZURE_CLIENT_ID — both were retired. The customer's
# setup script creates a user-assigned managed identity in THEIR OWN subscription with a federated-identity
# credential trusting the issuer (subject alethia-connector, audience api://AzureADTokenExchange); its
# client id is stored PER CONNECTION and the console + runner authenticate AS it via a minted assertion.
# NOTHING to set here — availability tracks the OIDC issuer key (parity with AWS/GCP/Alibaba).
# Alibaba is keyless + account-free: NOTHING to set here — the customer applies infra/connector/alibaba
# in their own account and connects with the role ARN. (Availability tracks the OIDC issuer key.)

# ── AI assistant (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The AI assistant / agent talks directly to configured model providers. Set
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and the AI **Free tier** runs in prod; leave it blank and AI stays off (routes
# 503, UI shows "not configured"). OPENAI_API_KEY is only needed if you point a role/override at an
# openai/* model. Paid AI tiers (Plus/Max) stay dark until the STRIPE_PRICE_AI_* prices below are set.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=   # optional — only for openai/* model overrides

# ── Stripe (inactive activation seam — leave blank) ─────────────────────────
# No paid consumer market is active. Do not populate these until commerce, tax, invoicing, and
# consumer-law readiness have been approved and the public terms have been updated.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
STRIPE_PRICE_TEAM=
# Metered prices for usage-based managed-runner minutes — without these, runner usage is metered
# but never charged. Create them as Stripe metered prices (event: alethia_runner_minutes).
STRIPE_PRICE_METER_TEAM=
STRIPE_PRICE_METER_ENTERPRISE=
# Standalone AI subscription prices — sell AI Plus / AI Max (raise the AI credit caps). Set at go-live;
# until set the paid AI tiers stay dark (AI Free needs no price and runs once ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set).
STRIPE_PRICE_AI_PLUS=
STRIPE_PRICE_AI_MAX=

# ── Support (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Slack incoming-webhook URL — staff get pinged on a new support case / customer reply. Unset → no ping.
SUPPORT_SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=
# Public community link (Discord/Slack/forum) on the in-app support page. Unset → the card is disabled.
# Comma-separated staff emails allowed into the admin.alethialabs.io support dashboard (behind
# Cloudflare Access). Unset → nobody can read cases there. e.g. borislav@alethialabs.io
SUPPORT_STAFF_EMAILS=

# ── Enterprise onboarding (operator plane) ───────────────────────────────────
# The ONLY external value the operator plane needs — everything else is wired automatically
# (PLATFORM_PROVISION_SECRET is [auto] via bootstrap-secrets.sh; PLATFORM_ADMIN_EMAILS +
# PLATFORM_SYSTEM_USER_EMAIL are const in the deploy assembler = the maintainer's account).
# The Stripe Product id enterprise line items reference (Stripe → Products → "Alethia
# Enterprise" → prod_…). Only needed for the Stripe-invoicing onboarding path; the off-Stripe
# path doesn't use it. Unset → the Stripe path errors with a clear message.
STRIPE_ENTERPRISE_PRODUCT_ID=

# ── Transactional email (hosted production) ─────────────────────────────────
# Hosted production temporarily uses Resend because SES production access was denied.
EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend
RESEND_API_KEY=
# Required public company-contact number rendered on /imprint.
ALETHIA_PUBLIC_PHONE=

# ── Status page box (optional; only if you run infra/status) ─────────────────
# The status box uses direct Caddy TLS (not the tunnel), so it needs an ACME email.
ACME_EMAIL=

# ── Analytics (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PostHog EU Cloud suite: consented analytics/funnels/Web Vitals/client errors, separately consented
# masked replay, and legitimate-interest server/migration diagnostics and structured operational logs.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://eu.i.posthog.com   # optional — default is https://eu.i.posthog.com
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_LOGS_ENDPOINT=
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_LOGS_HEADERS=
